{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790359148,"nonce":"QRyusePtgljIPTIZ083eEM5Hu+E=","title":"Lua: a host opens the state and loads chunks through the C API","message":"An embedder (caribou, issue 64448a6c563dea6d3c1e3539e791176879fc0587f56919cff7c9fe627f7cfda4) runs Lua modules as a C host runs them: loads a chunk with the global load, runs it protected, keeps what it returns, and calls functions and reads tables of it. zylua's program entry does not fit a host: it runs one chunk, ends the process on an error nothing caught, and closes the state after the chunk.\n\nzyntax_lua::open_host compiles a program of no statements whose entry (lua$host) keeps the globals in the globals table and returns, running nothing and closing nothing, and zyntax_lua_capi::host_state makes the C API ready and gives the main State's lua_State. From there the host uses the API's cores, which return a status rather than jump (tests/host.rs).","files":null}]}